"'''The Way You Move'''" is a song by the American [[Hip hop music|hip hop]] duo [[Outkast]], performed by its member [[Big Boi]]. The song features Outkast mentor [[Sleepy Brown]] on guest vocals. Along with "[[Hey Ya!]]", recorded by Outkast's other member [[André 3000]], "The Way You Move" served as the second single from Outkast's [[double album]] ''[[Speakerboxxx/The Love Below]]''.

Released from Big Boi's ''Speakerboxxx'' half of the double album by [[LaFace Records|LaFace]] and [[Arista Records]] on August 25, 2003, "The Way You Move" peaked at number one on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] the following year, becoming Outkast's third number-one pop single, and the 900th for ''Billboard''. In 2009, it was named the 22nd most successful song of the 2000s on the ''Billboard'' Hot 100 Songs of the Decade.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://www.billboard.com/bbcom/charts/chart_display.jsp?g=Singles&f=Greece#/charts-decade-end/hot-100-songs?year=2009&begin=21&order=position|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080610074032/http://www.billboard.com/bbcom/charts/chart_display.jsp?g=Singles&f=Greece#/charts-decade-end/hot-100-songs?year=2009&begin=21&order=position|url-status=dead|archive-date=June 10, 2008|title=Charts|magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]] |access-date=May 25, 2017}}</ref>

